DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddbbuuss--rruunn--sseessssiioonn is used to start a session bus instance of ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn
       from a shell script, and start a specified program in that session. The
       ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn will run for as long as the program does, after which it
       will terminate.

       One use is to run a shell with its own ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn in a text-mode or
       SSH session, and have the ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn terminate automatically on
       leaving the sub-shell, like this:

       dbus-run-session -- bash

       or to replace the login shell altogether, by combining ddbbuuss--rruunn--sseessssiioonn
       with the eexxeecc builtin:

       exec dbus-run-session -- bash

       Another use is to run regression tests and similar things in an
       isolated D-Bus session, to avoid either interfering with the "real"
       D-Bus session or relying on there already being a D-Bus session active,
       for instance:

       dbus-run-session -- make check

       or (in aauuttoommaakkee(1)):

             AM_TESTS_ENVIRONMENT = export MY_DEBUG=all;
             LOG_COMPILER = dbus-run-session
             AM_LOG_FLAGS = --

